properties.description:
skill_lint's DECISION_MATH_CONTRACT (tools/skill_lint.py, run in CI on every push, with its own tests in tools/test_skill_lint.py) pins six clauses in each of five served skills: capture-intent, brainstorm, detect-and-ask, revise-design and capture-session.
- name where each input came from;
- never your memory;
- compute in a calculator helper when one is connected;
- its kept record;
- linked with `documents`;
- otherwise show the arithmetic.
Matched case-insensitively with whitespace collapsed, so a line wrap or a sentence start cannot fail it. The same lint holds the .claude and .grok mirrors byte-identical to the source. What it cannot check is whether an agent actually keeps the math. That is judgement, and it stays evidenced by real use, as the file header says for every contract.
